Umbrella Facility for Gender Equality: The Umbrella Facility for Gender Equality (UFGE) is a multi-donor facility designed to strengthen awareness, knowledge, capacity for gender informed policymaking. The UFGE promotes results by equipping policy makers and development experts with data, knowledge, and evidence. The United Kingdom pledged $18,399,080. URL: http://wwwwds.worldbank.org/external/default/WDSContentServer/WDSP/IB/2015/11/18/090224 b0831c9f8e/2_0/Rendered/PDF/Partnering0for00program0report02015.pdf
Wealth Accounting and the Valuation of Ecosystem Services (WAVES) Multi-Donor Trust Fund: WAVES started in 2013 when countries signed a plan to conduct Natural Capital Accounting in their countries. The accounting framework is based on the System of Environmental and Economic Accounts (SEEA) approved by the United Nations Statistical Commission in 2013. The multi-donor trust fund was set up to assist the countries and researchers in developing WAVES. DFID pledged $3,747,540. URL:https://www.wavespartnership.org/sites/waves/files/kc/WAVES%20Annual%20Re port%202016_6.6.16.pdf


